@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-register`

-- g1-tests-register.l4: tests of g1-register.l4 (s.11).  Group G1.
-- Expected values are decided from the text of s.11 as printed (inputs/law.wiki lines 121 to 125, checked on gazette page 185)
-- before any rule was run: the register includes the licensee's details, the kind of licence and its validity period, and
-- any revocation or suspension; the register is open to the public by a query that states identifying details of the person.

§ `Tests of s.11`

§§ `The licences and their entries`

`the person p1` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "p1", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`the person p2` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "p2", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

`a grade 1 licence of p1` MEANS Licence WITH
    `the holder` IS `the person p1`
    `the kind of licence` IS `grade 1 licence`
    `a temporary licence under section 9` IS FALSE
    `granted on` IS YMD 2025 7 17
    `renewed on` IS EMPTY
    `validity ends on, as recorded` IS JUST (YMD 2030 3 31)
    `revoked on` IS NOTHING
    `suspended from` IS NOTHING
    `suspended until` IS NOTHING

`a revoked grade 2 licence of p1` MEANS Licence WITH
    `the holder` IS `the person p1`
    `the kind of licence` IS `grade 2 licence`
    `a temporary licence under section 9` IS FALSE
    `granted on` IS YMD 2025 8 1
    `renewed on` IS EMPTY
    `validity ends on, as recorded` IS JUST (YMD 2030 3 31)
    `revoked on` IS JUST (YMD 2027 1 15)
    `suspended from` IS NOTHING
    `suspended until` IS NOTHING

`a suspended grade 3 licence of p2 with no recorded end` MEANS Licence WITH
    `the holder` IS `the person p2`
    `the kind of licence` IS `grade 3 licence`
    `a temporary licence under section 9` IS FALSE
    `granted on` IS YMD 2025 9 1
    `renewed on` IS EMPTY
    `validity ends on, as recorded` IS NOTHING
    `revoked on` IS NOTHING
    `suspended from` IS JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)
    `suspended until` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)

§§ `s.11(a) what the register includes`

-- (1): the licensee's details, the kind of licence, and the validity period.
#ASSERT (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`)'s `the kind of licence` EQUALS `grade 1 licence`
#ASSERT ((`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`)'s `the details of the licensee`)'s `reference for the person` EQUALS "p1"
#ASSERT (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`)'s `the licence is valid until` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2030 3 31)
#ASSERT (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`)'s `the licence was granted on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 17
#ASSERT `s 11(a)(1) — the entry shows the validity period` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(a)(1) — the entry shows the validity period` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a suspended grade 3 licence of p2 with no recorded end`)

-- (2): the revocation or suspension of a licence.
#ASSERT `s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a revocation` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a revoked grade 2 licence of p1`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a revocation` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a revocation` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a suspended grade 3 licence of p2 with no recorded end`)
#ASSERT `s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a suspension` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a suspended grade 3 licence of p2 with no recorded end`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a suspension` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a suspension` (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a revoked grade 2 licence of p1`)
#ASSERT (`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a suspended grade 3 licence of p2 with no recorded end`)'s `suspended until` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)

-- The Registrar's duty to keep the register states no period.
#TRACE `s 11(a) — the Registrar must keep a register of licensees` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `keep a register of licensees` AT 20
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 11(a) — the Registrar must keep a register of licensees` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING

§§ `s.11(b) the register is open to a query that states identifying details`

`the whole register` MEANS
    LIST `s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`
       , `s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a revoked grade 2 licence of p1`
       , `s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a suspended grade 3 licence of p2 with no recorded end`

`a query naming p1` MEANS `Query of the register of licensees` WITH
    `identifying details of the person asked about were stated` IS TRUE
    `the reference for the person asked about` IS "p1"
`a query naming p2` MEANS `Query of the register of licensees` WITH
    `identifying details of the person asked about were stated` IS TRUE
    `the reference for the person asked about` IS "p2"
`a query naming a person with no licence` MEANS `Query of the register of licensees` WITH
    `identifying details of the person asked about were stated` IS TRUE
    `the reference for the person asked about` IS "p3"
`a query that states no details` MEANS `Query of the register of licensees` WITH
    `identifying details of the person asked about were stated` IS FALSE
    `the reference for the person asked about` IS "p1"
`a query with an empty reference` MEANS `Query of the register of licensees` WITH
    `identifying details of the person asked about were stated` IS TRUE
    `the reference for the person asked about` IS ""

#ASSERT `s 11(b) — the register shows, on a query` `a query naming p1` `the whole register` EQUALS RIGHT (LIST `s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a grade 1 licence of p1`, `s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a revoked grade 2 licence of p1`)
#ASSERT `s 11(b) — the register shows, on a query` `a query naming p2` `the whole register` EQUALS RIGHT (LIST `s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` `a suspended grade 3 licence of p2 with no recorded end`)
#ASSERT `s 11(b) — the register shows, on a query` `a query naming a person with no licence` `the whole register` EQUALS RIGHT EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 11(b) — the register shows, on a query` `a query that states no details` `the whole register` EQUALS LEFT `the query states no identifying details of the person asked about`
#ASSERT `s 11(b) — the register shows, on a query` `a query with an empty reference` `the whole register` EQUALS LEFT `the query states no identifying details of the person asked about`

-- The passive sentence read as a duty of the Registrar (callable, with no period): performed, or standing.
#TRACE `s 11(b) — the Registrar must open the register to public inspection by query, on the reading that the passive sentence implies a duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `open the register to public inspection by query` AT 15
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 11(b) — the Registrar must open the register to public inspection by query, on the reading that the passive sentence implies a duty` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
